## Align Home and Explorer e2e with current UI

Context: Playwright e2e on develop still expected the old Home 3-card workflow
strip and KPI counters, plus a "Knowledge Graph" sidebar label. The UI has
been All Domains + New Domain and "Explorer" since earlier branches; those
assertion updates never landed on develop, so the nightly e2e suite failed
on stale selectors. Unit contracts now pin the templates so routine pytest
catches the same drift without Playwright.

Changes:

1. tests/e2e/navigation/test_navigation_flows.py
   Replace workflow-card / classCount checks with the All Domains gateway
   and New Domain CTA.
2. tests/e2e/dtwin/test_dtwin_flows.py
   Accept the current Explorer sidebar label on the sigmagraph link.
3. tests/units/ui/test_home_and_explorer_contracts.py
   Pin home.html and menu_config.json so the old selectors cannot return
   unnoticed in routine runs.

Modified files:
- tests/e2e/navigation/test_navigation_flows.py
- tests/e2e/dtwin/test_dtwin_flows.py
- tests/units/ui/test_home_and_explorer_contracts.py

Tests: uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario" → 5763 passed, 304 skipped, 1 xfailed in 49.35s; targeted Playwright Home/Explorer e2e → 4 passed in 18.96s
